(6247681, 923568, 122131, '<td valign="top">I like the texture of the water, but would really like to see more details of the city.. The topic of the challenge is clearly stated as "Your challenge is to capture an image of which the horizon line is a dominant component."<br/>It looks like the foreground is dominant here, not the horizon -- I''m terribly sorry to mark this otherwise-great photo such low score.<br/>As it is, I''ll give it a 6.</td>', 'I like the texture of the water, but would really like to see more details of the city.. The topic of the challenge is clearly stated as "Your challenge is to capture an image of which the horizon line is a dominant component."It looks like the foreground is dominant here, not the horizon -- I''m terribly sorry to mark this otherwise-great photo such low score.As it is, I''ll give it a 6.', '2010-12-07 20:47:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247687, 923703, 122131, '<td valign="top">Wow.. I have such mixed feelings toward this shot..<br/>What a beautiful place, what amazing colours and textures on the clouds..<br/>You''ve framed the picture amazingly well and have captured the time perfectly.<br/>What a shame that the mountain range seems so over-processed.. To the point where it looks like a layer was applied over the mountains.. <br/>Perhaps the mountains were completely dark and you tried to lighten them up in post processing, and in the process you''ve lost pixel details..<br/>I don''t know..<br/>..... I''ll comment now, and will score at the end..<br/> <br/> <br/>** back to vote **<br/>Despite the beautiful clouds, my eyes keep getting drawn back to the mountains, and stopping me from enjoying the photo as it is meant to be.<br/>As such, I''ll score it a 7.</td>', 'Wow.. I have such mixed feelings toward this shot..What a beautiful place, what amazing colours and textures on the clouds..You''ve framed the picture amazingly well and have captured the time perfectly.What a shame that the mountain range seems so over-processed.. To the point where it looks like a layer was applied over the mountains.. Perhaps the mountains were completely dark and you tried to lighten them up in post processing, and in the process you''ve lost pixel details..I don''t know....... I''ll comment now, and will score at the end..  ** back to vote **Despite the beautiful clouds, my eyes keep getting drawn back to the mountains, and stopping me from enjoying the photo as it is meant to be.As such, I''ll score it a 7.', '2010-12-07 20:53:19.000000', NULL, 1),
